# Recorded dispositions for SOFT over-cap rows (TASK-384, ADR-048 amendment).
#
# One row per line: <path> -- <kind> -- <reason>, kind in: replace | merge | move-to-reference |
# automate-into-check | retain.  check-doc-caps reads this file and prints a NAMED `retained:` line
# for each disposed soft OVER-CAP instead of `OVER-CAP (soft)` -- never silently.  A row with no
# reason, an unknown kind, a duplicate path, or a STALE path (absent / mis-cased / ./-prefixed, no
# longer over its cap, or FROZEN) is itself a FAIL: a disposition that outlived its breach must not
# linger.  A HARD cap and the always-loaded token budget are NOT dispositionable -- a row naming a
# hard-capped path is reported and the hard FAIL stands (a promoted rule leaves CLAUDE.md through the
# `disposition:` pointer on its LEARNINGS line instead, see ADR-048 § Amended 2026-10-02).
#
# `retain` keeps the overage and so needs a real justification plus the condition that ends it; the
# other four kinds describe a move the file's diff must show.  A trim to squeeze under a cap is not
# a disposition ("not a diet").  The path is matched EXACTLY (trimmed, case-sensitive, no ./ prefix).

